        injectionType: "Manifold Injection. (This specific export variant utilizes specialized fuel lines, seals, and ECU mapping specifically designed to tolerate the high ethanol content (E20-E25) mandated in South American markets like Brazil. The injection pulse width and ignition timing are heavily altered to prevent detonation and corrosion from the alcohol-laced fuel.)",
        engineLifespan: "500,000+ km (Mechanically, the M111 cast-iron engine block is legendary. However, the lifespan in South American markets is often dictated by the quality of the local fuel and the harshness of the roads. The engine itself is practically immortal, but components like the fuel pump, fuel filter, and rubber fuel lines require closer attention due to the corrosive nature of high-ethanol fuel blends.)",
