          "Transmission Control Module Destruction: Capillary action from a leaking 13-pin connector on the 722.6 gearbox will push ATF into the passenger footwell, soaking and destroying the expensive TCM.",
          "Engine Misfire / Coil Degradation: Running old, worn-out spark plugs increases electrical resistance, which damages the waste-spark ignition coils. A failed coil will cause severe misfires and unburnt fuel to dump into the exhaust, destroying the catalytic converter.",
          "Overheating (Viscous Fan Clutch): The cooling system relies on a mechanical viscous fan clutch. As the fluid inside leaks out over the decades, the fan stops engaging at high temperatures, causing the engine to rapidly overheat in heavy traffic.",
