          "Vacuum System Leaks: The entire engine shut-off mechanism and transmission shifting (if automatic) rely on rubber vacuum lines. These lines crack with age, causing the engine to refuse to shut off when the key is removed, or causing harsh gear shifts.",
          "Glow Plug Seizure: The glow plugs frequently seize in the aluminum cylinder head due to carbon buildup. Attempting to force them out often snaps the plug, requiring expensive machine work to extract.",
          "Fuel Lift Pump Leaks: The mechanical lift pump attached to the injection pump uses rubber O-rings that dry out, introducing air into the fuel system and causing hard morning starts.",
          "W202 Chassis Rust: Catastrophic structural rust around the front spring perches, jacking points, wheel arches, and trunk.",
          "Engine Mount Collapse: The heavy cast-iron diesel engine vibrates significantly, completely crushing the fluid-filled engine mounts over time.",
