        injectionType: "Indirect Injection (Pre-chamber injection via a purely mechanical Bosch inline injection pump. This specific variant features a modified pump calibration designed to slightly restrict peak fueling, ensuring absolute maximum fuel economy and impenetrable longevity for fleet taxi operators in Spain and Portugal. It completely lacks complex electronics or ECU management.)",
        engineLifespan: "1 000 000+ km (The OM601 is globally recognized as one of the most indestructible internal combustion engines ever created. The cast-iron block and incredibly robust internal components are subjected to so little stress that wear is virtually nonexistent. This specific 72hp taxi variant was designed with one singular goal: to outlast the driver.)",
        turboType: "Naturally Aspirated (No turbocharger. The OM601 relies entirely on incredibly high 22.0:1 compression to generate its 123 Nm of torque. Power delivery is agonizingly slow, restricted even further by the fleet mapping, but completely linear and absolutely unstoppable.)",
        ecuType: "None (The engine management is purely mechanical. Fuel delivery is controlled by the Bosch inline pump, and essential functions like engine shut-off and idle speed adjustments are managed by rubber vacuum lines. There are no OBD codes or electronic Limp Modes to worry about.)",
